# Slab-only invariants

This rule is **not** symlinked. It only auto-applies when the agent
is operating inside `~/workspace/slab/` itself. Sibling projects
have their own `90-<project>-local.mdc`.

## Repo nature

Slab is a **personal knowledge base**, not application code. There is
no build, no test suite, no deployable artifact. The deliverables are
Markdown notes, design docs, Cursor skills/rules, and an occasional
canvas / HTML export. Treat all changes as documentation edits.

## Top-level layout (slab only)

```
AGENTS.md  README.md  .cursor/  knowledge/  papers/  notes/  weekly/  artifacts/  scripts/
```

Do not introduce new top-level directories without updating
`AGENTS.md` (`§3`) and this file.

## Commit & PR

- Default branch: `main`.
- Remote: `xmpeng-dev/system-lab` on GitHub.
- Large directory restructures (`git mv`) should be done with one
  logical group per commit so history stays bisectable.

## Things the agent must not do (in slab)

- Do not write into `.cursor/skills/` to record findings — that's what
  `notes/` and `knowledge/` are for. Skills hold reusable procedures
  only.
- Do not create new `summary/`, `docs/`, or sibling `README_<x>.md`
  files — they were deliberately retired in the May 2026 restructure.
- Do not touch `notes/<project>/raw/` (raw experiment logs are
  human-curated dumps; treat as read-only).
